Subject: [PATCH] pandora: defer the file pack with pandora_files_at, and log refused opens

Two things the last rounds could not see.

pandora_files_at=MS (bsd/dev/pandora_files.c): the installer always slept a fixed 2000 ms after
the root was mounted, so every file in the pack - including the 22 MiB NativeAdrenoMetal.bundle -
was in place long before Metal enumerates devices at about 14 s.  Metal then instantiates
NSPrincipalClass from the bundle, the accelerator cannot serve it, and backboardd freezes after
its fourth frame (SWEET FB: swap 4).  With the pack deferred, the bundle only appears once the
system is up, which is what the Trogdor port does by writing the plugin from an addon that
launchd mounts after boot.  Default unchanged (2000).

The open helper (iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp) refused any type other than 0x4147 and
printed nothing, so a refused IOServiceOpen looked exactly like an open that never happened -
and the whole discovery line was argued from that silence.  Log the refusal with the caller.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_files.c b/bsd/dev/pandora_files.c
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_files.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_files.c
@@ -125,7 +125,23 @@
 	for (int i = 0; i < 600 && rootvnode == NULLVP; i++) {
 		pf_sleep(500);
 	}
-	pf_sleep(2000);
+	/*
+	 * Patch 0336: pandora_files_at=MS defers the whole pack.  Installed late, the Metal plugin
+	 * bundle appears only after the system is up, so Metal's early device scan does not try to
+	 * instantiate a device whose accelerator cannot serve it (that scan hangs, and backboardd
+	 * freezes after its fourth frame).  Default stays 2000 ms as before.
+	 */
+	{
+		int at = 2000;
+		(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("pandora_files_at", &at, sizeof(at));
+		if (at < 0) {
+			at = 0;
+		}
+		if (at != 2000) {
+			printf("PANDORA FILES: pack deferred %d ms after root\n", at);
+		}
+		pf_sleep((unsigned)at);
+	}
 	uint8_t blk[4096];
 	uint32_t n = 0;
 	if (rootvnode == NULLVP || pandora_fw_read(0, blk, sizeof(blk))) {
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
@@ -548,6 +548,9 @@
 pandora_gpu_new_client(IOService *owner, task_t owningTask, void *securityID, UInt32 type, IOUserClient **handler)
 {
 	if (type != PANDORA_GPU_OPEN_TYPE && type != 0) {
+		char who[32];
+		proc_selfname(who, sizeof(who));
+		IOLog("PANDORA GPU ES: open type 0x%x refused for %s\n", type, who);
 		return kIOReturnUnsupported;
 	}
 	int c = pandora_gpu_open();
